    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "New to market. First open viewing Saturday 10th October 10-10.30am.\n\nGet Property Estate Agents are delighted to present this modern and inviting two-bedroom apartment, ideally situated in the heart of Chapelizod Village. Spanning 58 sq. m, No.85 Knockmaree is an exceptionally well-presented second-floor apartment, situated to the rear of the development enjoying highly attractive and peaceful views.\n\nConstructed in 2002, Knockmaree is an exclusive development set on a beautifully maintained site, conveniently located a stones throw from Chapelizod Main Street.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway with a generous storage room. The property further benefits from a modern open-plan kitchen, and a bright, spacious living area with access to a peaceful balcony. \nOff the hallway sits two well-proportioned bedrooms, both with integrated wardrobes with ample storage space, together with a stylish main family bathroom with a walk-in shower. \n\nACCOMODATION\nHallway: 3.40m x 0.96m. Wooden flooring. One storage room and home to hotpress with water tank.\nKitchen & living room: 7.80m x 3.65m. Modern kitchen, tiled flooring. Wooden flooring in living room, leading out to balcony.\nBedroom 1: 3.81m x 3.22m. Wooden flooring, leading out to rear balcony. Built-in wardrobes.\nBedroom 2: 3.83m x 2.10m. Wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes.\nBathroom: 2.11m x 1.77m. TIled floor to ceiling with walk in shower.\n\nMeasurements are for guidance purposes only.\n\nThe development is well managed and maintained by Cuala Property Management. The annual service charge for 2026 is approx. 2,275 including one designated car space, waste collection, block insurance, sinking fund and maintenance in the communal areas. \n\nThis spacious apartment is situated in the heart of Chapelizod. The Phoenix Park, Liffey walk and National Memorial Gardens are within a few minutes` stroll. It is just 7km from the city centre and is a short drive to the M50 and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre. \n\nChapelizod is a quiet village 6km west of Dublin city centre. It has a large convenience store, chemist, post office and a number of cafes, restaurants and pubs. The area still retains a peaceful village charm despite being so close to the city centre. A large number of buses pass through Chapelizod to the city centre with access to bus lanes for the majority of the journey. Cycling & walking paths leading to and from the city centre also enhance this residence`s location. The idyllic Strawberry Beds are located nearby. \n\nThe convenient location makes this apartment an ideal purchase for both first time buyers, downsizers and investors. Viewing is highly recommended. \n\nTo arrange a viewing please complete the form to the right of this page or give Michelle Hoare of Get Property Estate Agents a call on 086 032 8363.\n\nGet Property Estate Agents is fully licensed and regulated by the PSRA (002324).\n"
      },
